{"theorems":[{"slogan_id":8733566,"theorem_id":23832572,"name":"Corollary 4.7","body":"In a connected weighted undirected graph $\\Gamma $ with an edge $e=\\{ u,v\\} $, we have\\begin{equation*}  R_{e \\hspace{-.02in}f\\hspace{-.02in}f}(u,v)=\\frac{\\tau _{e}}{\\tau \\omega (e)}. \\end{equation*}","slogan":"The effective resistance between two connected nodes in a weighted graph equals the ratio of the number of spanning trees containing the edge to the product of the total number of spanning trees and the edge weight.","theorem_type":"corollary","label":null,"link":null,"paper":{"paper_id":"2109.01324v2","source":"arXiv","title":"Forest formulas of discrete Green's functions","authors":["Fan Chung","Ji Zeng"],"link":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2109.01324v2","summary":null,"journal_ref":null,"primary_category":"math.CO","categories":["math.CO"],"citations":0,"year":2022,"journal_published":true},"similarity":0.7557455578760298,"score":0.7557455578760298,"has_metadata":true},{"slogan_id":5199628,"theorem_id":20258646,"name":"Theorem 2.4 (\\cite{SR})","body":"Let $G=(V, E, \\{ w_e\\} )$ be a simple weighted graph with weight $w_{ij}=\\frac{1}{r_{ij}}$ if $ij\\in E$, and $w_{ij}=0$ if $ij\\notin E$, where $r_{ij}$ is the resistance of edge $ij\\in E$. For any two vertices $u, v\\in V$, the effective resistance between $u$ and $v$ is\\[ R_{uv}=\\frac{\\tau (G/\\{ u,v\\} )}{\\tau (G)}. \\]","slogan":"The effective resistance between two vertices in a weighted graph equals the ratio of the number of spanning trees in the graph with those vertices identified to the number of spanning trees in the original graph. The graph's edge weights are defined as the reciprocal of the resistances. This result connects graph theory with electrical network concepts. It provides a combinatorial formula for computing effective resistance.","theorem_type":"theorem","label":null,"link":null,"paper":{"paper_id":"1904.07766v1","source":"arXiv","title":"Spanning trees in complete bipartite graphs and resistance distance in nearly complete bipartite graphs","authors":["Jun Ge","Fengming Dong"],"link":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1904.07766v1","summary":null,"journal_ref":null,"primary_category":"math.CO","categories":["math.CO"],"citations":0,"year":2019,"journal_published":true},"similarity":0.7471198001146926,"score":0.7471198001146926,"has_metadata":true}]}